1
00:00:00,685 --> 00:00:02,165
(Sheldon:)Gentlemen, please.

2
00:00:02,320 --> 00:00:05,860
(Sheldon:)Leonard is trying to walk
a mile in my metaphorical shoes.

3
00:00:06,024 --> 00:00:08,164
(Sheldon:)He can't walk in my actual shoes.

4
00:00:08,326 --> 00:00:10,036
(Sheldon:)He has the feet of a toddler.

5
00:00:12,163 --> 00:00:15,163
(Raj:)So, how are you gonna return the DVD
if the store went out of business?

6
00:00:16,134 --> 00:00:19,544
(Leonard:)Monday morning I'll go downtown,
look up the owner's information,

7
00:00:19,704 --> 00:00:22,204
(Leonard:)send him the DVD.

8
00:00:24,542 --> 00:00:26,752
(Leonard:)Pay the late fee...

9
00:00:26,911 --> 00:00:29,051
(Leonard:)And prove to Sheldon
that you can have a problem...

10
00:00:29,214 --> 00:00:30,754
(Leonard:)And solve it...

11
00:00:32,384 --> 00:00:34,994
(Leonard:)Without acting
like a complete lunatic.

12
00:00:35,186 --> 00:00:36,356
Ahh!

13
00:00:37,722 --> 00:00:40,102
(Howard:)And the man impersonating a bear
would like everyone to know that,

14
00:00:40,258 --> 00:00:42,428
(Howard:)Only you can prevent forest fires.

15
00:00:45,397 --> 00:00:46,397
(Raj:)I don't get it.

16
00:00:47,065 --> 00:00:48,735
(Howard:)You didn't have
Smokey the Bear in India?

17
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:51,540
(Raj:)No. Oh, is he anything like
Mun-Mun the Mongoose?

18
00:00:53,204 --> 00:00:55,344
(Raj:)He taught us not to play with cobras.

19
00:00:57,042 --> 00:01:01,022
(Howard:)You had to be taught
not to play with cobras?

